cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this dataset or its findings, please cite it as below."
title: "bench-claude-arms: a controlled measurement of LLM coding-agent execution cost"
abstract: >-
  A pre-registered measurement of what it costs to run an LLM coding agent on a
  real Windows development machine. Four factors were varied: execution channel
  (CLI vs desktop application), delegation architecture (solo vs subagent
  delegation), reasoning effort (high vs medium), and task scale (a two-point
  dose-response). 22 task runs plus 2 instrument probes, USD 254.22, every run
  passing a pre-registered exclusion audit. Quality was held at a fixed contract
  and scored by a sealed held-out suite, so cost differences are read at equal
  contract-layer quality -- a qualifier the repository's rule file forbids
  dropping, because one arm scored full marks while shipping an unusable GUI.
  The repository publishes the raw run records and de-identified agent
  transcripts alongside the paper, so every figure can be re-derived.
type: dataset
